# Help: Rust XArray micro-benchmark module
#
# XARRAY_BENCHMARK_RUST builds the "xarray_benchmark_rust" module,
# which runs one workload through the Rust abstraction over the C
# XArray (kernel::xarray) and the same workload through the Rust
# XArray implementation (kernel::rxarray), and reports each timing to
# the kernel log. The run happens in module init and init then returns
# an error, so the module never stays loaded and every modprobe is one
# fresh run.
#
# The symbol is not in mainline yet: it arrives with the Rust XArray
# series. On a tree without it the requested value is ignored and the
# module is simply absent, so the fragment is safe to carry.
#
# Prerequisites inlined per the self-containment rule:
# RUNTIME_TESTING_MENU gates the whole menu, and RUST needs RANDSTRUCT
# disabled (rust/rust.config sets the same pair). MODULES comes from
# the base. The module is loaded on demand for a measurement, never at
# boot, so no builtin/ counterpart is needed.
# See: lib/Kconfig.debug (menu "Runtime Testing")
# See: https://docs.kernel.org/rust/
CONFIG_RUNTIME_TESTING_MENU=y
CONFIG_RANDSTRUCT_NONE=y
CONFIG_RUST=y
CONFIG_XARRAY_BENCHMARK_RUST=m
